sters\nRedis as metadata storage\n./weed version version 30GB 4.02 805950b401f9bf52424a6788c239d42dc6e1c666 linux amd64\n\n### Problem Description\nAfter deleting all objects in the bucket, the panel still shows that some objects still exist (after waiting for several hours).\n\n### steps\n\n1. Use `warp mixed` to write a 500KiB file. After the write is complete\n2. use `mc rm --recursive --force --dangerous seaweedhdd/sea` to delete all data.\n3. The admin UI page still displays data.\n### Related images\n\n<img width=\"1343\" height=\"577\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/20df6369-336b-4084-a390-930264a44a40\" />\n\n<img width=\"1299\" height=\"719\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1b9c307d-28de-47a5-96e7-62b9aa97d29a\" />\n<img width=\"361\" height=\"35\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/319e6e82-158f-49f7-88ac-6ee79237744e\" />\n\n<img width=\"1377\" height=\"705\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac8e0a10-aea9-4626-afaf-9d7d00635ddc\" />\n\n<img width=\"1358\" height=\"741\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/edb85a79-25d7-49c6-b6ac-8c183944ae8c\" />\n\n### Problems caused\n1. The volume cannot be reclaimed. I tried using ”fs.mergeVolumes“ to merge volumes, then “volume.vacuum” to delete the data, and finally “volume.deleteEmpty” to reclaim it, but it was ineffective.\n2. A lot of space is wasted。\n\nThere also appears to be an issue with inconsistent copy volume sizes:\n\n<img width=\"1218\" height=\"755\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c51aa370-d320-4e6a-b5d1-3abea4dd3a2e\" />\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/8168/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/8168/timeline","performed_via_